n status Messages Based On conditions 63abede \nDevice Configuration Paython commands fixes 914219a \nMerge pull request #86 from LiquiDynamics/19-webfcm-logic-needs-to-be-changed d0b9a13 \nMerge branch \'19-webfcm-logic-needs-to-be-changed\' of  https://github.com/LiquiDynamics/G2-Controller-PHP into 19-webfcm-logic-needs-to-be-changed b52c7d1 \nAdded PSM And CDM ID\'s in get_start_pump_response.php page 467205f \nMerge pull request #85 from LiquiDynamics/Development 51c77ec \nMerge pull request #84 from LiquiDynamics/19-webfcm-logic-needs-to-be-changed','global','E',0,1,1703082902,'G2'),(284,'version_39fzil','LQD_EG2_2_8','latest updates','global','E',0,1,1704374311,'G2'),(285,'version_6voi8v','LQD_EG2_2_9','Latest changes','global','E',0,1,1704982024,'G2'),(286,'version_0ujraw','LQD_EG2_2_10','CDM AND PSM ID missing related issue and removed few unwanted files','global','E',0,1,1705773669,'G2'),(287,'version_o6944e','LQD_E_2_100','Changes in start pump flow encase the FCM gets it command but the message doesn\'t get back to the controller and mim finds new value display messages but there is no t_dispense entry.','global','E',0,1,1706792671,'V1'),(288,'version_h8e4hs','LQD_E_2_101','commit \n01c4c0e','global','E',0,1,1707409225,'V1'),(289,'version_q2pczx','LQD_E_2_102','Commit 942b57c: 	Before enabling start button …. check fcm online or not, changes in error msgs. We have to stop command insertion if this option is off.tables and triggers need to be updated in the db vesion update sql	a. Track Device Status history trigger 	b. Trigger for Deleted Workorders c. Trigger for Deleted WorkOrder Details  SQL Triggers for t_server_transceiver and t_transceiver_server, updating user id and tech preset will now be updated by web','global','E',0,1,1707745806,'V1'),(290,'version_tci1vo','LQD_E_2_103','Fixes for missing successful pump start messages from FCM, updated a few items in the db tables that needed default values set on record creation.','global','E',0,1,1708023935,'V1'),(291,'version_nbd6b9','LQD_E_2_104','Using predispense timer for maximum amount of time it will check t_dispense table for record if successful pump start response message is lost.  Minor other bugs fixes.','global','E',0,1,1708348476,'V1'),(292,'version_gjcxjk','LQD_T_2_84','This test version is a duplicate of R_39.','global','T',0,1,1708530139,'V1'),(293,'version_k82miq','LQD_T_2_85','This is a test version of the software to fix when a start pump successful message is lost.  Identified at United BMW.  Commit 4606d35, #11, #30, back button greyed out but worked fix','global','T',0,1,1708531406,'V1'),(294,'version_4od0u3','LQD_E_2_105','d605a87 Fixed issues with calibration showing unsuccessful pump start when start response is missing. Resolved merge conflict in mim Commits on Feb 28, 2024 commented out the code that was putting a disp comp time in the t_dispense even if the disp amoutn was zero, auto_reset_reels and added some comments to CheckAutoClose, also change the timeout valu… Correct code for missing_startpump_response return values and stop setting disp completed time in t_dispnse table if disp amount is == 0. Added comment and error trapping in NewDisplayValue().\nCommits on Feb 27, 2024 Fixed bug where WO were not closing once dispense was completed. Referencing a global variable, not changing it, caused the error without declaring the global locally within the function.\nminor comment changes Commits on Feb 26, 2024 Added necessary code so that if start pump packet is lost AND the tech does not start dispensing but the PSM sends back a New Value packet within the 8 seconds, it will write a successful pump star… Added necessary code so that if start pump packet is lost AND the tech does not start dispensing but the PSM sends back a New Value packet within the 8 seconds, it will write a successful pump star…','global','E',0,1,1709227541,'V1'),(296,'version_9if8ir','LQD_E_2_106','Contains all the fixes for missed device messages during pump start communication, new workflow for work orders for MP and MD, db table changes which include default values for fields and the creation of table to track deleted workorders, past commands sent between web and middleware.','global','E',0,1,1718974154,'V1'),(298,'version_wan9ys','LQD_E_2_107','Fix for CDM with new serial chip, lost packets, MP and MD changes, CDM disconnect issue fix, TAC code fixes, new queries, debug code,','global','E',0,1,1720056242,'V1'),(299,'version_7c8bav','LQD_R_2_42','New CDM serial chip fix, MP and MD changes, TAC changes, new queries, debug code, mobile page fixes, missing packet fixes, device disconnected fixes, new db tables for tracking deleted wo and past server and transceiver commands, device status history.','global','R',0,1,1720058424,'V1'),(300,'version_zob1rn','LQD_R_2_43','Various debug statements added, comments to understand code, serial new chip code improved, device status history, web and serial command history, wo deleted history tracking added. MP and MD web work flow changed to match requests from customers.','global','R',0,1,1720661870,'V1'),(301,'version_ma5ee6','LQD_R_2_44','Added code to trap for CDM disconnection/failure so that log files do not fill up and it can gracefully recover from any serial errors.','global','R',0,1,1721419302,'V1'),(302,'version_dlisc1','LQD_R_2_45','Disabled debug variable serial_parse_debug and added if statement to trap for empty t_devices_software table.','global','R',0,1,1724242905,'V1'),(303,'version_2sn09c','LQD_R_2_46','restored R46 to listing.','global','R',0,1,1724243000,'V1'),(304,'version_vl0o48','LQD_E_2_108','Commented out blocks of code in mim that were doing crontab entry changes\n\nTo code that moves php.ini file from puthon to /etc/php5/apache2/ changed command from restart to do a stop then start command seperately with a 5 second sleep before restarting.\n\nCorrected incorrect entry in php.ini file for disable_functions as it showed php.ini at the end of the line but should have been phpinfo instead.','global','E',0,1,1731537195,'V1'),(305,'version_n993cv','LQD_E_2_109','Cleaned up db_version_update.sql made most entries into single line statements instead of being formated for easier reading/understanding as well as removed the statements where t_timeout_configuration was misspelled,t_timeout_configuaration.\nCommented out blocks of code in mim that were doing crontab entry changes\n\nTo code that moves php.ini file from puthon to /etc/php5/apache2/ changed command from restart to do a stop then start command seperately with a 5 second sleep before restarting.\n\nCorrected incorrect entry in php.ini file for disable_functions as it showed php.ini at the end of the line but should have been phpinfo instead.\n\nRemoved import of cron_manager\nRemoved global code for installing PTYZ each time MIM is started and instead just used the import pytz module.  Set global PYTZ_INSTALLED = 1.  When refactoring it is advised to remove all references to this vairable.\nAdded import teamviewer_control and signal\nSet global NEW_MODULE = 1\nSet global NEW_CONTROLLER = 1\nCommented out global index variable','global','E',0,1,1732191759,'V1'),(306,'version_0y7f5s','LQD_E_2_110','Removed from launcher the need to copy files to the www folder, added to the PATH the -var-www-oilcop-python- and added more error trapping. Changed permissions from 777 to 2775 and added feature to -\nCleaned up db_version_update-sql, made most entries into single line statements instead of being formatted for easier reading-understanding, and removed the statements where t_timeout_configuration -\nCleaned up db_version_update-sql, made most entries into single line statements instead of being formatted for easier reading-understanding.\nCorrected the spelling of t_timeout_configuration table in all files and corrected t_timeout_configuration_id field to f_timeout_configuration-id.\nUsing file Natesh created.\nAdded GetTimeoutValues-int-, removed Protocol_SetSystemTime-query-, updated networkchange-sh to remove the hardcoded value for new controller to accept a parameter from mim.\nUpdated mail_model-php to use port instead of host name.\nUpdated mail_model-php to use port info instead of server info to send either on port 587 or 465.\nMoved statements dated in the past to before the new changes.\nChanged start tank response to start pump response, added new condition for missing response packet entry to include whether or not dispense info is none.\nAdded function to remove all files from the UPDATES folder and remove all files - 90 days from the -var-www-logs folder.\nShell_command has been updated without params.\nBased on the host name, python or php mailers logic has been provided.\nFixed issues with device_status_unknown-callled_by- making it optional to pass the call procedure.\nAdded a sleep of 1 second before database connection attempt on startup.\nAdded an error if statement.\nThere were errors and missing triggers from one pushed to development.\nNatesh’s changes.\nAdded a test mail php file that works with the email_php-py file that can be used to confirm functionality of email credentials and server when email stops working.\nIndexing and query optimization queries update.\nDuplicate users display issue fix on email scheduler page.\nWhen deleting users, the data related to user roles should delete from role map table to avoid the duplicate emails list in the email scheduler page.\nPython mail library replaced with Phpmailer library.','global','E',0,1,1732285263,'V1'),(307,'version_zlveen','LQD_E_2_111','fixed conflictsGot the trigger creation in the db fixed using python code so removed them from the db_update_version.sql file.\nfixed issues with cron_manager.py and instead of rebooting change network settings using ifupdown command syntax.With launcher.sh: Ensured the script checks for root permissions.\nFixed the cron log timestamp escaping.\nImproved error handling with set -e and additional file existence checks.\nExplicitly redirected nohup output.\nClarified and cleaned up cd commands to avoid unnecessary state changes\nRemoved the function CSVFormatter() and just using basic logging formatter.\nRemoved timeout debug and info from displaying unless debug variable is set to true.\nchange the path for file permission from /var/www/oilcop to /var/www/\nAdded log cleanup to necessary files and removed commented out code that is no longer needed.','global','E',0,1,1732560900,'V1'),(308,'version_bxdvpk','LQD_E_2_112','294b3011 Fixed issues of cron commands being sent to parser one character at a time instead of the entire string.\nFixed permission typo in set_permissions()\nFixed but of multiple instances beging generated of mim. Replaced code to be compatible with py2.7.   Limited the commands passed to be run after updating crontab to the one that does not call the launcher_bash.sh file.\nAdded dos2unix program check and instllation in make_scripts_executable()\nAdded new file launcher_bash.sh so that when this update happens it uses bash for the luancher.sh instead of the sh interpreter.\nModified laincher.sh so that it uses the sh interpreter even though bash will run it there may be errors.\nModified MIM cron job for lanuncher.sh to call bash and launcher_bash.sh instead going forward.\nAdded feature to check_and_add_user_to_group() that will force the new group rights immediately if a user is added to a group.\nChanged the kill_processes() so that it runs after the run_crontab_commands() runs which will create duplicate instances of mim so new code will kill the lower PID which should be the old mim running.\nFixed logic bug for run_crontab_commands() where is was not parsing the cronjob correctly to get the command.','global','E',0,1,1733432110,'V1'),(309,'version_d8acq0','LQD_E_2_113','Added code to trap for disconnected/failing CDM issue.\nUpdate emai_php.py to accept parameters.\npython email script to replace php email script\nAdded a test mail php file that works with the emai_php.py file that can be used to confirm functionally of email credentials and server when email stops working.\nUpdated db_version_update_sql file so that triggers are correctly created in the DB.  Only the trigger for t_devices_software is currently not working but no code relies on this one as of yet\nPython mail library replaced with Phpmailer library\nWhen delete users, the data related to user roles should delete from role map table - to avoid the duplicate emails list in the email scheduler page\nDuplicate users display issue fix on email scheduler page\nIndexing and query optimization queries update\nFixed issues with device_status_unknown(callled_by) making it options to pass the call procedure.\nShell command has been updated without params\nChange start tank response to start pump response, added new condition for missing response packet entry to include whether or not dispense info is none.\nUpdated mail_model.php to use port info instead of server info to send either on port 587 or 465.\nUpdated db_version_update.sql to change Gartec email settings to use port 587 and STARTTLS instead of SSL and port 465.\nFix configuaration misspelling to configuration including the t_configuaration_id field name to f_configuration_id\nCleaned up db_version_update.sql file\nRemoved files from the www folder to prevent confusing with the master files in the www/oilcop/python folder.\nRemoved backup files\nAdded catch for hidden and folder from the updates folder no to remove them.  Only remove .zip files.\nFixed issue when system is set to Gartec or Admiral where t_dispense table is populated with the same user ID for every record.\nRemoved duplicate entries db_version_update.sql\nAdded a code comment to explain some defined global variables and track new module value','global','E',0,1,1736267624,'V1'),(310,'version_5f48w8','LQD_E_2_114','added a sleep of 1 second before database connection attempt on startup.\n\nFix configuaration misspelling to configuration including the t_configuaration_id field name to f_configuration_id\nCleaned up db_version_update.sql file\nRemoved files from the www folder to prevent confusing with the master files in the www/oilcop/python folder.\nRemoved backup files\n\nAdded catch for hidden and folder from the updates folder no to remove them.  Only remove .zip files.\n\nFixed issue when system is set to Gartec or Admiral where t_dispense table is populated with the same user ID for every record.\n\nRemoved duplicate entires in db_version_update.sql\n\nAdded a code comment to explain some defined global variables and track new module value\n\nAdded change so that TLS is set for oilcop email entry.  Set variable in email_php.py email_ssl to 0 as it was used for testing and now all emails use TLS and port 587.\n\nClarify subject email for high level warning and low level shutoff subject line changes\nRemoved required path for email_php.py to fix issues with not getting alert emails.\nCommented out unused variables SerialPort,2 in mim\nAdded some debug for scheduled email code in mim\nAdded debug with time when email scheduler is called from while true loop in mim\n\nChanged sql_insertDispenseAction name to sql_insertActionLog to match what it is actually doing which is logging into the action log.\nSet print statements for action and system logs to be displayed only if debug variable is set.\nChange LOG_ACCTION_DEBUG TO SYSTEM_LOG_DEBUG as that is how it was used\nReformatted serial open print statements to see why a serial read exception happens because there is no data in the buffer.\nRemoved variable cdm_communication_loss due to not being used from Open Serial function\nAdded clause to Serial read if statement to check if buffer has at least 32 bytes of data in it before reading to prevent read errors after reboots.\nAdded ifup and ifdown instead of using reboot on network changes.','global','E',0,1,1736768734,'V1'),(311,'version_dzka6v','LQD_E_2_115','added a sleep of 1 second before database connection attempt on startup.\n\nFix configuaration misspelling to configuration including the t_configuaration_id field name to f_configuration_id\nCleaned up db_version_update.sql file\nRemoved files from the www folder to prevent confusing with the master files in the www/oilcop/python folder.\nRemoved backup files\n\nAdded catch for hidden and folder from the updates folder no to remove them.  Only remove .zip files.\n\nFixed issue when system is set to Gartec or Admiral where t_dispense table is populated with the same user ID for every record.\n\nRemoved duplicate entires in db_version_update.sql\n\nAdded a code comment to explain some defined global variables and track new module value\n\nAdded change so that TLS is set for oilcop email entry.  Set variable in email_php.py email_ssl to 0 as it was used for testing and now all emails use TLS and port 587.\n\nClarify subject email for high level warning and low level shutoff subject line changes\nRemoved required path for email_php.py to fix issues with not getting alert emails.\nCommented out unused variables SerialPort,2 in mim\nAdded some debug for scheduled email code in mim\nAdded debug with time when email scheduler is called from while true loop in mim\n\nChanged sql_insertDispenseAction name to sql_insertActionLog to match what it is actually doing which is logging into the action log.\nSet print statements for action and system logs to be displayed only if debug variable is set.\nChange LOG_ACCTION_DEBUG TO SYSTEM_LOG_DEBUG as that is how it was used\nReformatted serial open print statements to see why a serial read exception happens because there is no data in the buffer.\nRemoved variable cdm_communication_loss due to not being used from Open Serial function\nAdded clause to Serial read if statement to check if buffer has at least 32 bytes of data in it before reading to prevent read errors after reboots.\nAdded ifup and ifdown instead of using reboot on network changes.\n\nAdded folder path to fil